    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        345,
        814,
        1221,
        1059
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "\"Section 1. There is hereby established under the direction of the Office of the Mayor a Commission on the Status of Women, which shall consist of thirty-eight members appointed by the Mayor, including a Chairperson and a Vice-Chairperson who shall serve at the pleasure of the Mayor, the Chairperson of the New York City Commission on Human Rights who shall serve ex officio and thirty-five members who shall serve as follows: twelve members shall be appointed for terms expiring on December 31, 1977; twelve shall be appointed for terms expiring on December 31, 1978; and eleven shall be appointed for terms expiring on December 31, 1979. Thereafter, all members other than the Chairperson, Vice-Chairperson and ex officio member shall be appointed for terms of three years. Should a vacancy occur prior to the expiration of the term of any member, such vacancy shall be filled for the unexpired term.\"",
